Z||000000||Rodney||11-21-2001||03:44 PM||||The lumbar parts quest is moving forward and will<BR>happen. I will have replacement bladders in possibly a<BR>month or two. They are looking into how hard it would<BR>be to set up and make a run of the original bladders<BR>from the original dies or if we will use ones that are<BR>very close that they can make quicker/easier.<P>The idea of putting together complete OEM retrofit<BR>lumbar kits is moving forward as well. But that will<BR>take some time. There are 2 pieces that have to be set<BR>up and run via an injection molder. After that is<BR>accomplished I should have complete kits soon after.<BR>Luckily that still have the injection molds. If they<BR>had tossed them this would have never happened. This<BR>may take 2-3 months yet. I have no idea on pricing as<BR>of yet.<P>Thanks,<BR>Rodney Dickman<BR>New web page! <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||11-21-2001||03:56 PM||||Rodney- Thanks for the update... I think the retro-fit kit will be a top seller! I can't wait to see what you come up with.  Keep up the great work.<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
